<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    "Add a place": the sub-screen reached from "+ ADD PLACE" in the Places tab's saved-places heading.

    **What the screen is for.** Saving the vet, groomer, park or shop — either the one the user is
    standing in, or any other point on Earth. Those are the two routes the map above the form offers,
    and they are equal partners: "I'M HERE" takes the device's position in one tap, and moving the map
    under its fixed centre pin chooses anywhere else. Whichever was used last is what gets saved; see
    PlaceLocationPicker.

    **Everything happens here.** There is deliberately no second "choose a location" page to go to and
    come back from: the map, its controls and the answer they produce all sit in this one scroll, above
    the fields that describe the place.

    Top to bottom:
      - **The shared header** (monogram, "Add place", theme toggle, pet count), fixed above the page as
        on the tabs. It is what keeps this screen recognisably part of the Places tab while the bottom
        bar keeps that tab lit.
      - Everything else scrolls as one page:
          · the **heading block** — a round back button beside "Add a place" and the sentence naming
            what the screen is for;
          · the **location picker** — the interactive map with "I'M HERE", the map-type menu, the fixed
            centre pin and the recentre control (see view_location_picker.xml);
          · the **selected-location card** — the address and coordinates under the pin
            (see view_selected_location.xml);
          · the **fields** — name, category, address, phone, opening hours, note. These are the same
            fields the full place form offers, so a place can be described completely as it is created
            rather than only afterwards;
          · the **summary** of what will be saved, then "SAVE PLACE".

    **What used to be here and is not.** A dark status card reporting on the GPS, with "Try again" and
    "Use demo location" beside it, sat between the map and the fields. The demo position is gone
    outright — a place saved at invented coordinates is indistinguishable from a real one, which makes
    it the most dangerous kind of placeholder — and the status reporting went with it, because with a
    movable map there is no longer a state in which the screen is stuck waiting for the sky. What
    replaced it answers the only question left: which place is about to be saved.

    **Why one NestedScrollView** rather than a RecyclerView for the page: the same reasoning as
    fragment_places.xml. These are a handful of stateful views, not rows. The map inside it keeps its
    own vertical drags — see PlaceMapView.onInterceptTouchEvent — so panning north does not scroll the
    form instead.

    **Why a CoordinatorLayout at the root:** so Snackbars attach here and appear above the floating
    bottom navigation bar rather than underneath it — see fragment_places.xml.
-->
<androidx.coordinatorlayout.widget.CoordinatorLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent"
    tools:context=".ui.place.AddPlaceFragment">

    <!-- The header takes the height it needs; the page takes the rest through height 0 + weight 1. -->
    <LinearLayout
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="match_parent"
        android:orientation="vertical">

        <!-- The shared header, as a nested binding (`binding.header`). -->
        <include
            android:id="@+id/header"
            layout="@layout/view_tab_header" />

        <androidx.core.widget.NestedScrollView
            android:id="@+id/addPlaceScroll"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="0dp"
            android:layout_weight="1"
            android:clipToPadding="false"
            android:paddingBottom="@dimen/add_place_scroll_padding_bottom">

            <LinearLayout
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:orientation="vertical"
                android:paddingStart="@dimen/screen_padding"
                android:paddingEnd="@dimen/screen_padding">

                <!-- ============================== Heading ==============================
                     The round back button and the text block beside it. gravity top rather than
                     centre, so the button lines up with the *first* line of a heading that wraps
                     rather than drifting down beside a two-line block. -->
                <LinearLayout
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/spacing_xs"
                    android:baselineAligned="false"
                    android:gravity="top"
                    android:orientation="horizontal">

                    <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
                        android:id="@+id/backButton"
                        style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.BackButton"
                        android:contentDescription="@string/cd_add_place_back" />

                    <LinearLayout
                        android:layout_width="0dp"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/spacing_md"
                        android:layout_weight="1"
                        android:orientation="vertical">

                        <!-- accessibilityHeading marks this as the page's heading, so TalkBack users
                             can jump straight to it with heading navigation. -->
                        <TextView
                            style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.Title"
                            android:layout_width="match_parent"
                            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                            android:accessibilityHeading="true"
                            android:text="@string/add_place_heading"
                            tools:targetApi="p" />

                        <!-- The moment the screen is for, in one line. -->
                        <TextView
                            style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.Subtitle"
                            android:layout_width="match_parent"
                            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                            android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/add_place_subtitle_gap"
                            android:text="@string/add_place_subheading" />

                    </LinearLayout>

                </LinearLayout>

                <!-- ========================== The location picker ==========================
                     The search field, the map and its four controls, shared with the full place form.

                     wrap_content, where this used to ask for the map's height: the picker is a column
                     now — a field with its suggestions hanging under it, above the map — and it holds
                     the map's fixed height internally. Asking for a height here would squash the
                     field or stretch the map. See view_location_picker.xml. -->
                <com.prash.petcare.ui.place.LocationPickerView
                    android:id="@+id/locationPicker"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/spacing_md" />

                <!-- The one line that says the map is a control rather than a picture. It has to be
                     said: a movable map looks exactly like a fixed one, and without this the only
                     position most users would ever save is the one the GPS handed them. -->
                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/mapHintText"
                    style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.MapHint"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/spacing_sm"
                    android:text="@string/map_picker_hint" />

                <!-- What the pin is pointing at, in words and figures. -->
                <include
                    android:id="@+id/selectedLocation"
                    layout="@layout/view_selected_location"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/spacing_md" />

                <!-- ============================ The save fields ============================
                     The same set the full place form offers, so that everything a saved place can be
                     edited to hold can also be given at the moment it is created — see requirement 15.
                     Only the name and a location are required; the rest can be left for later, which
                     is what keeps the two-tap save from becoming a form to fill in. -->

                <TextView
                    style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.FieldLabel"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:text="@string/add_place_name_label" />

                <com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputLayout
                    style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.Field"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content">

                    <!-- capWords because a place name is a proper noun. -->
                    <com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputEditText
                        android:id="@+id/nameInput"
                        style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.NameInput"
                        android:layout_width="match_parent"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:hint="@string/add_place_name_hint"
                        android:imeOptions="actionNext"
                        android:inputType="textCapWords" />

                </com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputLayout>

                <TextView
                    style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.FieldLabel"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:text="@string/add_place_category_label" />

                <!-- Vet · Grooming · Park · Store. The Tasks tab's filter chips, built in code from
                     PlaceCategory — see ui/common/FilterChips.kt — so the chosen pill gets exactly the
                     treatment every other chosen thing in the app does. A wrapping ChipGroup rather
                     than a scrolling row: four short pills fit two-and-two on the narrowest phone, and
                     a category hidden off the edge of a scroller is one that never gets chosen. -->
                <com.google.android.material.chip.ChipGroup
                    android:id="@+id/categoryChipGroup"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    app:chipSpacingHorizontal="@dimen/spacing_sm"
                    app:selectionRequired="true"
                    app:singleSelection="true" />

                <!-- The address. Filled in from the map's own lookup and editable afterwards — see
                     AddPlaceViewModel.onAreaChanged for how a typed answer stops the lookup writing
                     over it. -->
                <TextView
                    style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.FieldLabel"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:text="@string/place_area_label" />

                <com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputLayout
                    style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.Field"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content">

                    <com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputEditText
                        android:id="@+id/areaInput"
                        style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.NoteInput"
                        android:layout_width="match_parent"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:hint="@string/add_place_area_hint"
                        android:imeOptions="actionNext"
                        android:inputType="textPostalAddress|textCapWords"
                        android:maxLines="1" />

                </com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputLayout>

                <!--
                    The place's number: a country selector and the local number beside it, exactly as
                    the full place form draws them.

                    Optional — many parks have none — but a number that *is* given is stored in one
                    international form and checked against the country chosen, because the saved-place
                    row offers to dial it. The behaviour behind the pair is ui/common/PhoneNumberInput.kt,
                    shared with the sign-in and profile forms.

                    A horizontal LinearLayout: the selector at a fixed width so the number box always
                    starts in the same place whatever the dialling code, and the number taking the rest
                    (width 0 + weight 1).
                -->
                <TextView
                    style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.FieldLabel"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:text="@string/place_phone_label" />

                <LinearLayout
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:baselineAligned="false"
                    android:orientation="horizontal">

                    <!-- Not typed into: tapping it opens the country list. PhoneNumberInput makes it
                         unfocusable and gives it a spoken description naming the country in full. -->
                    <com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputLayout
                        android:id="@+id/phoneCountryLayout"
                        style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.Field"
                        android:layout_width="@dimen/phone_country_field_width"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content">

                        <com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputEditText
                            android:id="@+id/phoneCountryInput"
                            style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.NoteInput"
                            android:layout_width="match_parent"
                            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                            android:inputType="none"
                            android:maxLines="1"
                            tools:text="🇳🇵 +977" />

                    </com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputLayout>

                    <!-- inputType="phone" brings up the dial pad. How many digits it accepts is capped
                         per country by PhoneNumberInput, so an over-long number cannot be typed. -->
                    <com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputLayout
                        android:id="@+id/phoneInputLayout"
                        style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.Field"
                        android:layout_width="0dp"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/phone_country_field_gap"
                        android:layout_weight="1"
                        app:errorEnabled="true">

                        <com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputEditText
                            android:id="@+id/phoneInput"
                            style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.NoteInput"
                            android:layout_width="match_parent"
                            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                            android:hint="@string/add_place_phone_hint"
                            android:imeOptions="actionNext"
                            android:inputType="phone"
                            android:maxLines="1" />

                    </com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputLayout>

                </LinearLayout>

                <!-- ============================ Opening hours ============================
                     Opens and Closes side by side, each half the width through layout_weight — they
                     are one fact ("8:00 to 20:00") and read best on one line. Tapping either opens a
                     Material time picker; focusable="true" with the soft keyboard suppressed in code
                     keeps them reachable by keyboard and switch access without popping up a keyboard. -->
                <TextView
                    style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.FieldLabel"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:text="@string/place_hours_heading" />

                <LinearLayout
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:baselineAligned="false"
                    android:orientation="horizontal">

                    <com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputLayout
                        style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.Field"
                        android:layout_width="0dp"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_weight="1">

                        <com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputEditText
                            android:id="@+id/openingTimeInput"
                            style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.NoteInput"
                            android:layout_width="match_parent"
                            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                            android:clickable="true"
                            android:cursorVisible="false"
                            android:focusable="true"
                            android:hint="@string/place_opening_label"
                            android:inputType="none"
                            android:maxLines="1" />

                    </com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputLayout>

                    <com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputLayout
                        style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.Field"
                        android:layout_width="0dp"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/spacing_sm"
                        android:layout_weight="1">

                        <com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputEditText
                            android:id="@+id/closingTimeInput"
                            style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.NoteInput"
                            android:layout_width="match_parent"
                            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                            android:clickable="true"
                            android:cursorVisible="false"
                            android:focusable="true"
                            android:hint="@string/place_closing_label"
                            android:inputType="none"
                            android:maxLines="1" />

                    </com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputLayout>

                </LinearLayout>

                <!-- One error for the pair rather than one per field, because the problem ("only one
                     of the two is set") belongs to neither field alone. -->
                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/hoursErrorText"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/spacing_xs"
                    android:textAppearance="?attr/textAppearanceBodySmall"
                    android:textColor="?attr/colorError"
                    android:visibility="gone"
                    tools:visibility="visible" />

                <!-- For places with no opening hours, such as a public park. -->
                <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
                    android:id="@+id/clearHoursButton"
                    style="@style/Widget.Material3.Button.TextButton"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:text="@string/place_clear_hours"
                    android:visibility="gone"
                    tools:visibility="visible" />

                <TextView
                    style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.FieldLabel"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:text="@string/add_place_note_label" />

                <com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputLayout
                    style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.Field"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content">

                    <!-- imeOptions actionDone, since this is the last field on the form. -->
                    <com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputEditText
                        android:id="@+id/noteInput"
                        style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.NoteInput"
                        android:layout_width="match_parent"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:hint="@string/add_place_note_hint"
                        android:imeOptions="actionDone"
                        android:inputType="textCapSentences" />

                </com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputLayout>

                <!-- ============================ Summary and save ============================
                     Two lines: what is about to be saved, and the position it will carry — the exact
                     coordinates once a point has been chosen, and a line saying so until then. The
                     second line is the screen's honesty about itself, shown before the user commits.

                     accessibilityLiveRegion polite: it changes as the form is filled in, and a screen
                     reader should mention the change without interrupting what is being typed. -->
                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/summaryText"
                    style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.Summary"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/spacing_lg"
                    android:accessibilityLiveRegion="polite"
                    tools:text="Untitled place · Vet\nNo location chosen yet" />

                <!-- Disabled until the place has both a name and a location. Disabled here means a
                     solid resting slab with pale ink, not a faded button — see attrs.xml,
                     colorDisabledContainer — and the label says which of the two is missing. -->
                <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
                    android:id="@+id/savePlaceButton"
                    style="@style/PetCare.AddPlace.SaveButton"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/spacing_md"
                    tools:text="@string/add_place_save" />

            </LinearLayout>

        </androidx.core.widget.NestedScrollView>

    </LinearLayout>

</androidx.coordinatorlayout.widget.CoordinatorLayout>
